ion': 'Multiplying a varying indicator (2,4,6) by a constant (3) should produce (6,12,18).'}]}, {'group': 'Null argument handling', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'this', 'value': 'NumericIndicator.of(ConstantIndicator(DecimalNum.valueOf(1)))'}, {'parameter': 'other', 'value': 'null'}], 'expected': 'NullPointerException', 'description': 'Calling multipliedBy with a null indicator must throw a NullPointerException.'}]}, {'group': 'Identity multiplication (self * self)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'this', 'value': 'NumericIndicator.of(ConstantIndicator(DecimalNum.valueOf(7)))'}, {'parameter': 'other', 'value': 'NumericIndicator.of(ConstantIndicator(DecimalNum.valueOf(7)))'}], 'expected': 'NumericIndicator whose getValue(i) == DecimalNum.valueOf(49) for any i', 'description': 'Multiplying an indicator by itself should square its values (7 * 7 = 49).'}]}, {'group': 'Multiplication of two varying indicators', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'this', 'value': 'ClosePriceIndicator(series) where series values are [1, 2, 3]'}, {'parameter': 'other', 'value': 'VolumeIndicator(series) where series values are [10, 20, 30]'}], 'expected': 'NumericIndicator whose getValue(0) == DecimalNum.valueOf(10), getValue(1) == DecimalNum.valueOf(40), getValue(2) == DecimalNum.valueOf(90)', 'description': 'Both operands vary per bar; product should be element‑wise multiplication of close price and volume series.'}]}, {'group': 'Multiplication with negative and zero values in varying indicators', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'this', 'value': 'ClosePriceIndicator(series) where series values are [-5, 0, 5]'}, {'parameter': 'other', 'value': 'ClosePriceIndicator(series) where series values are [2, -2, 0]'}], 'expected': 'NumericIndicator whose getValue(0) == DecimalNum.valueOf(-10), getValue(1) == DecimalNum.valueOf(0), getValue(2) == DecimalNum.valueOf(0)', 'description': 'Both indicators contain negative and zero values; the product must reflect sign rules and zero propagation.'}]}, {'group': 'Multiplication involving derived indicators (HighestValueIndicator)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'this', 'value': 'HighestValueIndicator(series, 2) where series values are [1, 3, 2, 5]'}, {'parameter': 'other', 'value': 'ConstantIndicator(DecimalNum.valueOf(2))'}], 'expected': 'NumericIndicator whose getValue(0) == DecimalNum.valueOf(2), getValue(1) == DecimalNum.valueOf(6), getValue(2) == DecimalNum.valueOf(6), getValue(3) == DecimalNum.valueOf(10)', 'description': 'Highest value over the last 2 bars yields [1,3,3,5]; multiplied by 2 the expected series is [2,6,6,10].'}]}, {'group': 'Chained operations resulting indicator multiplication', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'this', 'value': 'NumericIndicator.of(ConstantIndicator(DecimalNum.valueOf(2))).plus(ConstantIndicator(DecimalNum.valueOf(3)))'}, {'parameter': 'other', 'value': 'ConstantIndicator(DecimalNum.valueOf(4))'}], 'expected': 'NumericIndicator whose getValue(i) == DecimalNum.valueOf(20) for any i', 'description': '((2 + 3) = 5) * 4 = 20; verifies that chaining of plus() followed by multipliedBy() yields the correct constant result.'}]}, {'group': 'Commutativity check between two indicators', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'this', 'value': 'ClosePriceIndicator(series) where series values are [1, 4]'}, {'parameter': 'other', 'value': 'ConstantIndicator(DecimalNum.valueOf(5))'}], 'expected': 'Both a.multipliedBy(b) and b.multipliedBy(a) produce NumericIndicator whose getValue(0) == DecimalNum.valueOf(5), getValue(1) == DecimalNum.valueOf(20)', 'description': 'Multiplication should be commutative; swapping operands must not change the resulting series.'}]}, {'group': 'Mismatched series length handling', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'this', 'value': 'ClosePriceIndicator(seriesA) where seriesA values are [1, 2]'}, {'parameter': 'other', 'value': 'ClosePriceIndicator(seriesB) where seriesB values are [10]'}], 'expected': 'IndexOutOfBoundsException when getValue(1) is called on the resulting indicator', 'description': 'When the two underlying indicators have different bar counts, accessing an index that exists only in the longer series should raise an IndexOutOfBoundsException.'}]}]
